schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: ProjectTogether used pay-after-results funding for 2022 Ukraine refugee relief
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    In 2022, ProjectTogether coordinated Ukraine refugee relief where funders
    paid after seeing the work done, so resources flowed based on
    demonstrated need rather than upfront promises.
  evidence: >-
    Stated as a standalone example in impact-certificates-hypercerts.md's
    "How Retroactive Funding Works" section, with no citation or link
    provided.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/impact-certificates-hypercerts.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used by the article as a concrete illustration of retroactive funding
    working in a real humanitarian-response context.
  uncertainty: >-
    No source is cited for this example (the article has no References
    section); the specific mechanism, funders, and outcome were not
    independently verified for this ingestion.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/impact-certificates-hypercerts.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
